drm: sun50i-h713-afbd: keep the panel in the record's window words

With 0117 the firmware rebuilds its window chain on a geometry change, and it
runs the rebuild twice. Read out of its own log at level 5, the first pass is
correct and the second is not:

    pass 1   capture_cfg [1280,720][1280,720]  display_cfg [1920,1080][1920,1080]
             ProcWinNode in [1280,720] out [1920,1080]  ratio [43690 x 43690]
    pass 2   capture_cfg [ 853,480][1280, 720]  display_cfg [1280, 720][1920,1080]
             ProcWinNode in [ 852,480] out [1280, 720]

The difference between them is which record they saw. Pass 1 still ran against
the old record, whose window words held the panel, so the capture size came
from the signal and everything lined up. Pass 2 ran against the new one, whose
window words held the source -- and the window manager reads those words
straight into m_src_cfg, then maps the capture into them with CalcPropRect.
1280 * (1280/1920) = 853, 720 * (720/1080) = 480. That is the smeared band on
the wall, and the 0x1E0 and 0x36 in the INCAP registers.

So words 2..5 follow the source, because they are the frame the AFBD hands
over; words 28..34 stay the panel, because they are the window manager's
configuration and not a geometry at all. Outside ring mode both stay the plane's
own size, where there is no second geometry to confuse them.

The mapping is read back out of the running firmware, not inferred: publishing
w = 1280 made m_src_cfg read [0, 0, 20480, 11520], and 20480 is 1280 * 16.

diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c	2026-09-07 22:48:35.517800337 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c	2026-09-07 22:48:35.524593254 +0200
@@ -288,7 +288,8 @@
  * firmware was not measured against is left at zero.
  */
 static void h713_afbd_build_video_info(u32 *rec, unsigned int w,
-				       unsigned int h, unsigned int stride)
+				       unsigned int h, unsigned int stride,
+				       unsigned int win_w, unsigned int win_h)
 {
 	memset(rec, 0, H713_VIDEO_INFO_WORDS * sizeof(*rec));
 
@@ -311,10 +312,22 @@
 	rec[24] = 0;			/* SDR */
 	rec[25] = 0;			/* no HDR metadata buffers */
 	rec[26] = 0;
-	rec[28] = w * 16;		/* display window, 1/16 pixel */
-	rec[30] = h * 16;
-	rec[32] = w * 16;
-	rec[34] = h * 16;
+	/*
+	 * These four are NOT the frame geometry -- they are the window manager's
+	 * configuration, and it reads them straight into m_src_cfg and m_dst_cfg
+	 * (measured through the firmware's shell: publishing w = 1280 put
+	 * [0, 0, 20480, 11520] there, which is 1280 and 720 in 1/16 pixel).
+	 *
+	 * They have to stay the panel. When they carried the source instead, the
+	 * firmware's proportional mapping (CalcPropRect) shrank the capture by
+	 * the ratio between them and the panel: a 1280x720 source came out as
+	 * 853x480 and the picture was a smeared band. With the panel here, the
+	 * capture size comes from the signal, which is where it belongs.
+	 */
+	rec[28] = win_w * 16;		/* window config, 1/16 pixel */
+	rec[30] = win_h * 16;
+	rec[32] = win_w * 16;
+	rec[34] = win_h * 16;
 }
 
 /*
@@ -423,7 +436,9 @@
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	new_ptr = readl(h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_INFO0) != ptr;
-	h713_afbd_build_video_info(rec, w, hgt, stride);
+	h713_afbd_build_video_info(rec, w, hgt, stride,
+				   ring ? h->mode.hdisplay : w,
+				   ring ? h->mode.vdisplay : hgt);
 	differs = memcmp(h->video_info, rec, sizeof(rec)) != 0;
 	write_record = differs && (!h->video_info_published || ring);
 	if (differs && h->video_info_published && !ring)
